/favicon.svg       /favicon.svg       200
/coming-soon.html  /coming-soon.html  200

# Netlify serves an existing file instead of a plain 200 rewrite, so the catch-all
# has to be forced (200!) or the live pages stay up. Cloudflare Pages rejects 200!
# and ignores that line; the plain 200 rule under it is the one Pages uses.
# Pages also strips .html and would loop on a rewrite to /coming-soon.html, so the
# Pages rule targets /coming-soon, which resolves to this same file.
